cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this formalization, please cite it as below, together with the
  paper it formalizes. Scott Armstrong was supported by the European Research
  Council (ERC) under the European Union's Horizon Europe research and
  innovation programme, grant agreement No. 101200828. Vlad Vicol was
  partially supported by the Collaborative NSF grant DMS-2307681 and by a
  Simons Investigator Award.
title: "AVAnomalousDiffusion: a Lean 4 formalization of anomalous diffusion by fractal homogenization"
version: "1.0"
date-released: 2026-10-02
abstract: >-
  A machine-checked Lean 4 / Mathlib formalization of S. Armstrong and V.
  Vicol, "Anomalous diffusion by fractal homogenization". For every alpha in
  (0, 1/3) it constructs a divergence-free, alpha-Hölder drift on [0,1] x T^2
  for which the advection-diffusion equation exhibits anomalous dissipation
  for every mean-zero H^1 datum, the solutions are uniformly Hölder in time
  with values in L^2 along a set of diffusivities accumulating at zero, and
  vanishing-diffusivity limits are not unique. The proof uses only the
  standard axioms; corrections to the paper are documented in the
  repository.
type: software
